    <string name="rx_empty_hero_title">Official NIH RxNav &amp; RxNorm Directory</string>
    <string name="rx_empty_hero_desc">RxNorm provides normalized names and unique identifiers (RxCUI) for medicines produced by the U.S. National Library of Medicine (NLM). Searching here retrieves exact RxCUIs required for reliable multi-drug interaction screening.</string>
    <string name="rx_what_is_rxcui">What is an RxCUI?</string>
    <string name="rx_what_is_rxcui_desc">An RxNorm Concept Unique Identifier (RxCUI) is a standardized numerical code assigned to each distinct clinical drug. Healthcare systems and clinical decision support tools use RxCUIs to cross-reference drug combinations, detect dangerous adverse contraindications, and prevent medication errors.</string>
